From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:15:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: configure session picker sort and filter

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Allow configuring session picker sort order and
default filter
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 1006-personal-feature-configure-session-picker-sort-and-filter.patch

Patch intent:
Add configurable sorting and default filter for the session picker,
controlling the initial sort order and filter applied when opening the
picker.

Why it exists:
The session picker defaults were not configurable, forcing users to
manually re-sort and filter on each use.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs,
crates/jcode-tui/src/tui/session_picker.rs and its configured-picker
child test module, and crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs.
The inline-interactive resume paths use
set_current_dir_with_configured_filter to preserve directory setup ordering.

Update guidance:
Keep the sort and filter configuration options in the session picker
section of the config. Preserve the default values when options are
unset.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-tui session_sort_orders_by_the_configured_field --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui sort_ordering_applies_to_filtered_rows --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui sort_ordering_applies_to_saved_sessions_in_grouped_view --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui sort_ordering_is_consistent_across_loaded_and_cache_reloaded_lists --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui default_filter_current_dir_shows_only_matching_sessions_after_set_current_dir --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui default_filter_all_shows_every_session --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui default_filter_current_dir_applied_on_async_loaded_picker --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui default_filter_current_dir_preserved_on_async_reseeded_picker --lib
